# Family OS — current execution guard

Before significant work, read `PROJECT_EXECUTION_PLAN.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/CURRENT_EXECUTION_PLAN.md`, and the authorization/runtime-truth documents they name.

- Do not revive a phase, backlog card, loop state or scope claim from `docs/archive/`.
- The active increment is the controlled synthetic Children Roster staging release. A local test or CI pass is not deployment or staging-verifier evidence.
- Do not add Flutter remote integration, a second client API read, provider expansion, device/native enforcement, recovery/support scope, real data, production or public release without a separate decision.
- Preserve truthful UX: a real vertical slice includes role/scope authorization, source/freshness visibility, loading/empty/error/denied/pending/recovery states, accessibility, responsive behavior and RTL/EN quality.
- Never put credentials, database URLs, JWTs, identities, raw provider responses or real family data in source, Git, CI, docs or chat.
- Use only reviewed forward migrations; never migrate at application startup, in a build step or in CI.
